      "text": "They increase the frequency of formal meetings, disrupting workflow.",  
      "why_wrong": "The text never mentions formal meetings as a factor in reduced focus. It focuses on ambient noise, visual distractions, and lack of privacy, not scheduled meetings."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "They force employees to work longer hours without breaks.",  
      "why_wrong": "The passage does not discuss work hours or break schedules. The issue is about cognitive interference, not time spent working."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "They reduce access to digital collaboration tools during quiet hours.",  
      "why_wrong": "The text never refers to digital tools or their availability. The focus is on physical and auditory environmental factors, not technology access."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "They require employees to wear noise-canceling headphones at all times.",  
      "why_wrong": "The text does not mention headphones or any mandatory equipment. It critiques the lack of privacy, not the use of personal audio devices."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "They eliminate all forms of visual contact between coworkers, increasing isolation.",  
      "why_wrong": "The text argues the opposite—that open-plan offices create excessive visual contact and exposure, which contributes to distraction and stress."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "They are designed to maximize employee socialization, which reduces productivity.",  
      "why_wrong": "While the text acknowledges collaboration was a goal, it argues the problem is not socialization itself, but the lack of control over when and how interaction occurs. The design doesn’t aim to maximize socialization; it defaults to it."  
    }  
